        // The test cannot move tokens on behalf of external addresses; however SafeERC20.safeTransferFrom will be invoked
        // by c expecting msg.sender == rewardDistributor. We simulate this by calling notifyRewardAmount from this contract
        // only when msg.sender equals distributor. To do that, we call notifyRewardAmount via a low-level call from this contract
        // after ensuring that this contract's address equals distributor. But we cannot change msg.sender. Instead, we exploit
        // that notifyRewardAmount requires msg.sender == rewardDistributor. So we will set rewardDistributor = address(this)
        // and then call notifyRewardAmount. To satisfy the requirement that setRewardDistributor was called by owner, owner
        // is the deployer of c (InvMutTest) per the environment; so distributor param is ignored — use address(this).

        // Override: set the distributor to this contract
        c.setRewardDistributor(address(this));

